G2443.def:
**ἵνα**,
I. _adverb_ (poët., Hom., al.),
1. of place, **where, whither**.
2. of circumstance, **when**.
II. _Conjunction_,
1. prop., final, denoting purpose or end (cl.), **that, in order that**, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (cl. also) preceded by an emphatic word ([[Act.19.4|Act.19:4]], [[Rom.11.31|Rom.11:31]] (?), [[Gal.2.10|Gal.2:10]], al.);
(a) with optative (so in cl. after historic tenses): after a pres., [[Eph.1.17|Eph.1:17]] (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2);
(b) with subjc.: after a pres., [[Mrk.4.21|Mrk.4:21]], [[Luk.6.34|Luk.6:34]], [[Jhn.3.15|Jhn.3:15]], [[Act.2.25|Act.2:25]], [[Rom.1.11|Rom.1:11]], al.; after a pf., [[Mat.1.22|Mat.1:22]], [[Jhn.5.23|Jhn.5:23]] [[1Co.9.22|1Co.9:22]], al.; after an imperat. (present or aor.), [[Mat.7.1|Mat.7:1]], [[Mrk.11.25|Mrk.11:25]], [[Jhn.10.38|Jhn.10:38]], [[1Co.7.5|1Co.7:5]], al.; after a delib. subjc., [[Mrk.1.38|Mrk.1:38]], al.; after a fut., [[Luk.16.4|Luk.16:4]], [[Jhn.14.3|Jhn.14:3]], [[1Co.15.28|1Co.15:28]], al.; after historic tenses (where optative in cl.; WM, 359f.; M, _Pr._, 196f.), [[Mrk.6.41|Mrk.6:41]] (impf.), [[Jhn.4.8|Jhn.4:8]] (plpf.), [[Mrk.3.14|Mrk.3:14]] (aor.), al.;
(with) in late writers (M, _Pr._, 35; Burton, §§198, 199), with indic., fut: [[Luk.20.10|Luk.20:10]], [[1Pe.3.1|1Pe.3:1]], al.;
(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, see word), with indic. pres.: [[1Co.4.6|1Co.4:6]], [[Gal.4.17|Gal.4:17]], al. (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.);
(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: [[Jhn.18.37|Jhn.18:37]], [[1Ti.1.16|1Ti.1:16]], al.; τούτου χάριν, [[Tit.1.5|Tit.1:5]]
(f) **elliptical constructions**: omission of the principal verb, [[Jhn.1.8|Jhn.1:8]], [[2Th.3.9|2Th.3:9]], [[1Jn.2.19|1Jn.2:19]], al.; of the final verb, [[Rom.4.16|Rom.4:16]], [[2Co.8.13|2Co.8:13]], al.
2. In late writers, definitive, = inf. (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), **that**;
(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, etc.: θέλω, [[Mat.7.12|Mat.7:12]], al.; ζητῶ, [[1Co.4.2; 14.12|1Co.4:2 14:12]]; ζηλόω, [[1Co.14.1|1Co.14:1]], al.;
(b) **after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting**: εἰπεῖν, [[Mat.4.3|Mat.4:3]], al.; ἐρωτῶ, [[Mrk.7.26|Mrk.7:26]], al.; παρακαλῶ, [[Mat.14.36|Mat.14:36]], [[1Co.1.10|1Co.1:10]], al., etc.;
(with) after words expressing expediency, etc.: συμφέρει, [[Mat.18.6|Mat.18:6]], [[Jhn.11.50|Jhn.11:50]], al.; ἱκανός, [[Mat.8.8|Mat.8:8]], [[Luk.7.6|Luk.7:6]]; χρείαν ἔχω, [[Jhn.2.25|Jhn.2:25]], al, etc.;
(d) **after substantives, adding further definition**: ὥρα, [[Jhn.12.23; 13.1|Jhn.12:23 13:1]]; χρόνος, [[Rev.2.21|Rev.2:21]] συνήθεια, [[Jhn.18.39|Jhn.18:39]] μισθός, [[1Co.9.18|1Co.9:18]]
3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, **that, so that** (M, _Pr._, 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): [[Rom.11.11|Rom.11:11]], [[1Co.7.29|1Co.7:29]], [[1Th.5.4|1Th.5:4]], al. (but see Thayer, see word); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, [[Mat.1.22; 2.14|Mat.1:22 2:14]], [[Jhn.13.18|Jhn.13:18]], al.
(AS)

G2448.def:
**Ἰούδα**, (a) Ἰουδαῖος, ὁ, **a Jew**: [[Jhn.4.9|Jhn.4:9]], [[Act.18.24|Act.18:24]], [[Rom.2.28|Rom.2:28]]; pl., [[Rev.2.9; 3.9|Rev.2:9 3:9]]; οἱ Ἰ., [[Mat.2.2|Mat.2:2]], [[Mrk.7.3|Mrk.7:3]], [[Jhn.2.6|Jhn.2:6]], al.; Ἰ. τε καὶ Ἕλληνες, [[Act.14.1|Act.14:1]], al.; κ. προσήλυτοι, [[Act.2.10|Act.2:10]] ἔθνη τε κ. Ἰ., [[Act.14.5|Act.14:5]] οἱ κατὰ τὰ ἔθνη, [[Act.21.21|Act.21:21]] of Jewish Christians, [[Gal.2.13|Gal.2:13]] of the ruling class who opposed Jesus, [[Jhn.1.19; 2.18; 5.10; 11.8; 13.33|Jhn.1:19 2:18 5:10 11:8 13:33]], al.;
(b) Ἰουδαία, -ας, ἡ (sc. γῆ, χώρα, cf. [[Jhn.3.22|Jhn.3:22]], [[Mrk.1.5|Mrk.1:5]]), (Heb. יְהוּדָה), **Judæa**: [[Mat.2.1|Mat.2:1]], [[Luk.1.5|Luk.1:5]], [[Jhn.4.3|Jhn.4:3]], al.
(AS)
